.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Jul 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-chains - List supported blockchains (chain IDs used in --chain-id)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 chains [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the blockchains supported by the environment.

.PP
Filter with --symbol (the chain's native symbol, e.g. ETH / USDC / CELO) and/or
--network-type (testnet | mainnet). Both match case-insensitively; combine them
to narrow further.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for chains

.PP
\fB-n\fP, \fB--network-type\fP=""
	Filter by network type: testnet or mainnet

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--symbol\fP=""
	Filter by native symbol (e.g. ETH, USDC, CELO)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 chains
  rail0 chains --symbol USDC
  rail0 chains --network-type testnet
  rail0 chains -s ETH -n mainnet
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0(1)\fP
